.TH AMAYA 1 "" "Amaya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amaya \- privacy-first web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amaya
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURL\fR|\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amaya
is a privacy-first web browser built on Mozilla's Gecko engine.
It accepts the same command-line options as Firefox.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window \fIURL\fR
Open \fIURL\fR in a new window.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-tab \fIURL\fR
Open \fIURL\fR in a new tab.
.TP
.B \-\-private\-window [\fIURL\fR]
Open \fIURL\fR in a new private window.
.TP
.B \-P [\fIPROFILE\fR]
Start with \fIPROFILE\fR, or show the profile manager.
.TP
.B \-\-ProfileManager
Start with the profile manager.
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Disable extensions and themes for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without a user interface.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the full list of options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/amaya/
Application directory.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/amaya/distribution/policies.json
Enterprise policies shipped with Amaya.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR x-www-browser (1)
